 - 2026-06-15: PHASE A2 (THE HEADLINE GATE, gated_on A1 selector_trained) -- does the ORACLE-DISTINCT learned ARC verifier BEAT majority vote OFF-ORACLE? On a HELD-OUT ARC split (disjoint from A1 folds), rerank with the A1 learned verifier (verifier_is_oracle=false; does NOT execute demos) vs majority-vote vs a MATCHED no-verifier control (same candidates/budget) vs oracle@K (the positive-control ceiling) vs an ARBITER conservative-override arm (keep vote unless the learned margin clears a fixed threshold, arXiv:2605.26172 / AggLM 2509.06870). The LOAD-BEARING gate: verifier@1 - vote@1, bootstrap CI95 EXCLUDES 0 AND headroom exists. YES -> the first oracle-distinct verifier win (closes GAP-3-ties-vote; informs the DiffusionGemma gate). TIE-with-headroom -> honest null. No-headroom -> uninformative (FALSE_NEGATIVE_RISK, not a verifier failure). (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: oracle_distinct_verifier_ties_vote_with_headroom; results/experiment_4221_oracle_distinct_arc_verifier_beats_vote.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE B1 (HARNESS-FIRST, the .360 discipline) -- FIX + SMOKE the LoRA training harness that died 3x. .390's exp4211 failed with `ValueError: Target module Gemma4ClippableLinear(...) is not supported` -- PEFT/LoRA matched the custom Carnot Gemma4 wrapper (whose .linear submodule is the real nn.Linear) instead of a standard module. FIX: load the NON-Qwen base via standard transformers.AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained('google/gemma-4-E4B-it') (NOT the custom Gemma4 wrapper) so PEFT sees standard nn.Linear, with explicit target_modules (q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj/gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj) -- OR unwrap/patch the wrapper to expose its inner .linear. DELIVERABLE = a PASSING SMOKE (a positive control ON THE HARNESS): assert LoRA attaches, 1 training step runs, loss is finite, on a 8-16-example fixture from the intact corpora. NO full 3-arm run here (that is B2). harness_smoke_passed BARE bool. NO TRM. (❌ Failed) — honest_verdict=failed: verifier_reward_lora_harness_smoke_failed; results/experiment_4222_verifier_reward_lora_harness_fix_smoke.json
 - 2026-06-15: PHASE B1 (HARNESS-FIRST, the .360 discipline) -- FIX + SMOKE the LoRA training harness that died 3x. .390's exp4211 failed with `ValueError: Target module Gemma4ClippableLinear(...) is not supported` -- PEFT/LoRA matched the custom Carnot Gemma4 wrapper (whose .linear submodule is the real nn.Linear) instead of a standard module. FIX: load the NON-Qwen base via standard transformers.AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained('google/gemma-4-E4B-it') (NOT the custom Gemma4 wrapper) so PEFT sees standard nn.Linear, with explicit target_modules (q_proj/k_proj/v_proj/o_proj/gate_proj/up_proj/down_proj) -- OR unwrap/patch the wrapper to expose its inner .linear. DELIVERABLE = a PASSING SMOKE (a positive control ON THE HARNESS): assert LoRA attaches, 1 training step runs, loss is finite, on a 8-16-example fixture from the intact corpora. NO full 3-arm run here (that is B2). harness_smoke_passed BARE bool. NO TRM. (✅ Complete) — honest_verdict=complete: verifier_reward_lora_harness_smoke_passed; results/experiment_4222_verifier_reward_lora_harness_fix_smoke.json
